ther or and not anyways etc)) they don't spawn too much, so these are quite conservative tweaks but significant. With also buildings like the [LINK=BUILDING_HARBOR]harbor[\LINK] quite strongly buffed (view sevopedia for details) now, water planting should be a strong alternative to purely land ones, especially to complete an otherwise nice land location but poorer in ressources. I tried to make sure naval planting doesn't become too op or the opposite for land, i hope more versatility and strategy(ies? Anyways etc) can be used now as part of this rework, as well as more accurate gameplay. On that note, some pedia entries have been updated, [LINK=BONUS_WHALE]whales[\LINK] have been buffed too, etc, please view for details sevopedia bonus or/and docs or/and other pages anyways etc (or don't blame me if not accurate info you have hehe if i may say but do as you prefer here is all the info i have or most that was not too tedious or forgetted or rather forgotten xd if i may say but anyways etc of me to say but anyways etc... I hope gameplay will or and can be more interesting now with these balance changes without skewing too much at one side or the other, and that now there are more possibilities to play civ4 in a balanced perhaps competitive way, at least in theory and to best i could do at least of now, hopefully enjoyable or and helpful or not at least to me, may be tweaked in the future or and not, anyways etc.[NEWLINE]- Made ressources/bonuses generally spawn more towards the edges of the map, it was a bit too skewed towards central spawning for most bonuses, giving central start too big of an advantage over edge start, hopefully and with other bonuses and changes to spawn rate and such a bit closer now or/and balanced anyways etc[NEWLINE]- Shrines now require to also have the corresponding religion as a prequirement to build them (and not only just the holy city as before, which is still required now), this means for example that if you conquer a holy city that doesn't have a shrine, you can't build the shrine until/unless you have the matching religion if i am not mistaken (for example to build the [LINK=BUILDING_DAOIST_SHRINE]Daoist Shrine (Currently named "The Dai Miao" as of now (i.e. (as of?) me writing this (sevopedia) doc) anyways etc)[\LINK] you need to have the [LINK=RELIGION_DAOISM]"Daoism"[\LINK] religion too. This allows to display shrines in sevopedia and perhaps also makes more sense in terms of gameplay if it doesn't create issues hopefully, trying it to see anyways etc, see sevopedia entries or/and project/mod docs for details[NEWLINE]- Shrines now also require a tech to be built, which is their religion's tech requirement. This allows to make shrines to also appear in tech tree, plus now shrines cannot be built without also having the religion's tech matching (for example during conquest or such, anyways etc), since shrines are not special buildings unlike temple, monastery, cathedral, maybe this is a fine even desirable way to handle it (in tech tree display, also about the conquest thing or similar or other issues or examples of what may happen but anyways etc as these are world wonders unlike the temple, the monastery, and the cathedral), tech prerequirement for shrines was NONE. See also docs for details or related issues/fixes/reworks ('s) info anyways etc.[NEWLINE]- Removed religion "confucianism", added [LINK=RELIGION_PAGANISM]religion "paganism"[\LINK], more popular and relevant for civ4 maybe as many leaders were religious if i am not mistaken but with no religion, see notes_about_religious_design.txt for details in the docs online on github or(/and(anyways etc)) offline in this project files too for details[NEWLINE]- Fixed and ajusted many religious inaccuracies of favourite religions, at least those i spotted with (being) certainty (certain enough) maybe anwyas etc (or not or/and other or/and not anways etc), for example frederick the great was agnostic not christian, brennus more leaning non religous than pagan (not inaccurate since paganism didn't exist but may fix other xml related fields or maybe not such as religion preference or not anwyays etc), and genghis khan, while tengrist something and not strictly daoist, expressed or/and showed(?) a strong respect(/liking?) for (a(/the?)) daoist leader, so his favourite religion can be assessed to be daoism, especially if he had to choose between civ4 only religions, here being none or daoism, he leans more strongly -much mroe if i am not mistake but anyways etc) towrds daoism), so a leader can have a favourite religion without it being their religion of themselves, see notes mentionned above for details, and this is all if i am not mistaken, but (i thnk)(and hope but anyways etc) if this is (and i was) accurate enouh (but anyways etc) hopefuly accurate enough and (much maybe(?) maybe or not or/and other or not anyways etc) accurate now hopefully maybe or not or/and other or/and not (but) anwyays etc[NEWLINE]- Barbarians are now much stronger in the early game economically, they should now grow at a similar pace than human and other players too until the middle game where they will gradually fade. They should also spawn cities more often and be relevant longer in the game, even though for now at least if not always or not they have trouble to grow past a certain size, and are still not a real player (no diplomacy and scattered cities that are independent, but that contribute together to the "barbarian(s?)((,)'s) civilization"), and become a key part in politics or invasion decisions, maybe i mean or not or/and other or not anyways etc. Their (now new)(anyways etc) overall strength increase (for example they are also harder to kill at all difficulties (less to no combat bonus against them, but never reverse bonus to them to make the game fair and balanced and fun as much as possible at least to me or and maybe (to) others ideally or maybe not (and or maybe not ideally or not or other or and not anyways etc) but anwyays etc) is gradual with difficulties), and they should not be (too) op though so hopefully not overbearing either but demanding more strategy or/and attention to hopefully make the game interesting, while filling some unsettled areas if not claimed fast enough in a quite realistic way too maybe anyways etc. They are also more calculating in who they attack, may raze cities much more than in base AdvCiv/Civ4 if am not mistaken anyways, and are more calculating in who they attack target the weak not the strong, anyways etc, or/and other changes or and not anyways etc. See [LINK=CIVILIZATION_BARBARIAN]Barbarians (Civilization)[\LINK] for details ingame or/and the XML for example for the Steam version of the game (adjust to where your AdvCiv-SAS mod is if path is different or/and you don't use the Steam version of the game) C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Sid Meier's Civilization IV Beyond the Sword\Beyond the Sword\Mods\AdvCiv-SAS\Assets\XML\Civilizations\CIV4CivilizationInfos.xml and related files like CIV4BuildingInfos.xml and CIV4HandicapInfo.xml or/and such.[NEWLINE][NEWLINE][BOLD]Fixes[\BOLD][NEWLINE]- Fixed a seemingly AdvCiv/Civ 4 bug where Gandhi's nowar attitude prob were pleased(110) / pleased(115) instead of (seemingly how should be if i am not mistaken anyways etc) pleased(110) / friendly(115)[NEWLINE]- (Seemingly now) Fixed a seemingly bug in base AdvCiv/Civ4 where barbarians could build shwedagon paya or mausolleum of mausollos for example (maybe other wonders too, and national wonders too like moai and hermitage etc) as happened in auto play, sometimes even completing them, by using iBuildUnitProb 100 or a similar high value (was 0 in base AdvCiv code or/and civ4 code anyways etc but anyways etc), seems to be extremely effective, testing more to be sure. Note: I had(have? Anyways etc) tried other approaches like iWonderConstructRand -9999 on LEADER_BARBARIAN in leader head infos xml file, or FLAVOR_MILITARY 10 but did not work at all it seems. I also removed all old logic of buildingclass NONE that seemed to not have any effect on wonder building whether it was here (national wonders) or not (removed it for world wonders, but sitll exact same results it seems of wonders being built, sometimes completed even anyways etc), maybe such barbarian wonder building behaviour/tendency/possibility was just suppressed because barbarians did not grow fast enough to support as in encourage as in do wonder building (activites) anyways etc, but now that they grow fast enough at human and other player's pace, they can make wonders or attempt to, which "derails" from their original warmongering goal and intent in AdvCiv-SAS but anyways, so refraining them from doing it, anyways etc anyways etc...[NEWLINE]- Fixed a seemingly AdvCiv/Civ 4 bug of Sevopedia Unit's placeRequires's Religion button (for example any religious missionary unit) not redirecting to sevopedia religion (nothing happens on click anyways etc), by replacing, in sevopediaunit py file, in placeRequires function/method (of this file anyways etc), WidgetTypes.WIDGET_HELP_RELIGION with WidgetTypes.WIDGET_PEDIA_JUMP_TO_RELIGION(,) as is done already by base advciv and successfully in sevopedia building, anyways etc anyways etc anyways etc[NEWLINE]- Rebalanced great artist: nerf/reduce early bomb culture instant culture gain from 700 to 500 per era, and increase culture per turn for long term victory culture path or and other uses from 12 to 20 per turn, see sevopedia ingame or xml for latest values if they changed in the meantime and i didn't (re)update them here anyways etc (anyways etc), anyways etc</English>
